Before initiating sub-agent workflows, classify the user's objective:

| Mode | Trigger / Criteria | Pipeline Execution & Output Scope |
|---|---|---|
| **Mode A: Full Archaeological Discovery** | New codebase onboarding, comprehensive audit, or full repo intelligence request. | Run Full 5-Stage Pipeline across whole repo: `repo-analyst` &rarr; `arch-mapper` &rarr; `code-inspector` &rarr; `modernizer` &rarr; `validator`. Outputs to `docs/`. |
| **Mode B: Single-Feature Vertical Slice Extraction** | User requests extraction of a specific feature, workflow, or slice (e.g., **Login Flow**, **MFA / 2FA Challenge**, **Registration**, **Checkout**). | Run Feature-Scoped Pipeline: All sub-agents isolate and trace *only* the components, routes, domain services, database tables, and rules for that feature. Outputs to `docs/features/<feature-slug>/` (or scoped `docs/`). |
| **Mode C: Targeted Contract / API Extraction** | User requests endpoint discovery, data model extraction, or business rule auditing for a specific module. | Targeted Run: `repo-analyst` (brief scan) &rarr; `code-inspector` &rarr; `validator` (scoped). |
| **Mode D: Modernization & Reconstruction** | Migration, framework upgrade, cloud re-platforming, or microservice decomposition. | Run Full Pipeline with heavy emphasis on `modernizer` target mapping and risk mitigation. |
| **Mode E: Architectural & Flow Mapping** | Dependency analysis, boundary audit, or Mermaid sequence/topology mapping. | Scoped Run: `repo-analyst` &rarr; `arch-mapper` &rarr; `validator`. |

