## 3. Single-Feature Vertical Slice Protocol (Mode B)

When the user requests extracting a single feature (e.g., *IdentityServer Login*, *MFA Verification*, *User Registration*, *Order Checkout*):

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    REQ["User: 'Extract Login Flow'"] --> SCOPE["Orchestrator: Define Feature Boundary\n(Slug: 'login-flow')"]
    SCOPE --> F1["Phase 1: repo-analyst (Feature Slice)\n- Identify routes: /account/login, /auth/token\n- Identify feature dependencies & configs"]
    F1 --> F2["Phase 2: arch-mapper (Feature Lifecycle)\n- Map sequence diagram for Login\n- Map boundaries: Ingress -> AuthSvc -> UserStore -> TokenEngine"]
    F2 --> F3["Phase 3: code-inspector (Feature Contracts & Logic)\n- Extract DTOs, credential hashing, lockout rules\n- Extract DB tables: Users, Credentials, AuditLog"]
    F3 --> F4["Phase 4: modernizer (Feature Reconstruction Blueprint)\n- Self-contained, portable specification\n- Decoupled interface so feature can run standalone"]
    F4 --> F5["Phase 5: validator (Feature Isolation Audit)\n- Verify zero missing dependencies in slice\n- Check all error branches (lockout, invalid pwd)"]
    F5 --> DONE["Delivery: docs/features/login-flow/\nComplete, self-contained, reimplementable!"]
```

### Key Requirements for Feature Slice Extraction:
1. **Complete Vertical Boundary:** Trace from the public trigger (HTTP route, UI controller, API endpoint) down to domain services, external integrations (SMS, SMTP, OAuth providers), database tables, and outgoing tokens/cookies.
2. **Exhaustive Branch Coverage:** Capture both happy path and all error/edge paths (e.g. invalid credentials, unverified email, account locked, MFA required, remember-me cookie generation, session expiration).
3. **Self-Contained Extraction:** The resulting `reconstruction-spec.md` must specify everything needed to implement this feature as an independent module or microservice without dragging in unrelated monolith code.

