## 5. Structured Sub-Agent Delegation Protocol

When delegating a task to a sub-agent, use this standardized task payload:

```markdown
### Sub-Agent Task Dispatch: <agent-name>
- **Task ID:** TASK-<number>
- **Target Agent:** <repo-analyst | arch-mapper | code-inspector | modernizer | validator>
- **Scope & Mode:** <Whole Repository | Feature Slice: e.g., "Login Flow">
- **Feature Focus (if applicable):** <e.g., "Extract only Authentication & Login Flow (routes, handlers, credentials store, token generation)">
- **Inputs & Prior Artifacts:**
  - <List relevant prior docs, e.g., docs/inventory.md or docs/features/login/inventory.md>
- **Key Constraints:**
  - Anchor every finding with file paths and line numbers.
  - Do not guess; mark unknown logic as [UNVERIFIED].
- **Output Artifact Destination:** <e.g., docs/features/login/contracts.md>
```

When receiving the sub-agent's response, require the standardized Handoff Contract:
```markdown
### Agent Handoff: <agent-name>
- **Status:** COMPLETED | INCOMPLETE | BLOCKED
- **Confidence Level:** HIGH | MEDIUM | LOW
- **Feature Scope:** Whole Repo | <feature-name>
- **Artifacts Emitted:** <list of generated or updated files>
- **Key Findings:** <concise summary of 3-5 major discoveries>
- **Identified Gaps / Unknowns:** <list of unresolved questions or unverified areas>
- **Next Recommended Step:** <recommended next agent or action>
```

